Z||000000||Cheever2||01-18-2001||01:00 PM||||I really hate posting this, cuz I KNOW it's a stupid question.  But Napa says they have to order it, and I don't wanna be calling a hunnert shops to find one.  Your advice?<BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||3400Fiero||01-18-2001||01:13 PM||||I replaced my leaking heater core with one from my local auto wrecker<P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Oreif||01-18-2001||02:39 PM||||I had a dealer install mine. A relative works at a Pontiac dealership and he checked the parts counter. They had one in stock. I was charged $175.00 for the part and installation, But now I have the "Goodwrench" lifetime warranty. (If it goes bad they replace it. The part is free but I have to pay labor) When mine went bad I called around and every place said I had to Order it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||01-18-2001||02:41 PM||||Autozone, Checker/Kragens/Grand Auto, Napa all have to order it so get it where it is the cheapest, cause it likely comes from the same distributor anyway.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||01-18-2001||03:11 PM||||Bought all of mine at Autozone...around $25 if I recall and a pretty easy fix to.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||01-18-2001||08:52 PM||||I put a Modine in mine over the summer. I forget what it cost. I think I ordered it thru wrenchead or carparts.com... Modine is a very well established line.<P>I won't put in a used core. Used ones are all to often on their way south already. <P>||||reg||1
